course: dictionary
lesson: 13840
title: Jettison: throwing things away
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Jettison is a verb, a doing word. It means to throw something out, often to make a load lighter. «The crew had to jettison the empty fuel tanks to make the rocket lighter.» The clue is lighter: the crew got rid of something heavy.
explain: Look at the words around it. «In the storm, the sailors jettisoned the heavy crates of cargo over the side.» Storm and heavy tell you that jettisoned means thrown overboard. Test your meaning in the sentence: "threw the heavy crates out" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Jettison can also be used for ideas. «We should jettison this plan, because it is not useful.» Nothing is thrown into the sea here. It means to drop an idea or give it up because it is not useful. The clue is not useful, so the plan is dropped.
fact: Jettison means to throw something out, often to make something lighter.
fact: «Jettison» is a verb: jettisons, jettisoned, jettisoning.
fact: Rockets can jettison empty fuel tanks, and ships and planes can jettison cargo.
fact: «Jettison» can also mean to drop an idea or plan because it is not useful.
fact: Jettison is often used when there is an emergency, when quick action is needed.
exercise: «The crew had to jettison the empty fuel tanks.» What does jettison mean here? | To paint and decorate | To fill up with more fuel | *To throw out, to make the rocket lighter | To wait quietly on the ground
exercise: «The sailors jettisoned the heavy crates in the storm.» Why did they do it? | *To make the ship lighter and safer | To sell the crates for money | To hide them from the captain | To take a nap
exercise: «We should jettison this plan, because it is not useful.» What does jettison mean in this sentence? | To shout it to everyone | To write the plan down neatly | To keep it safe forever | *To drop the idea and give it up
test: «In an emergency, the pilot had to jettison the heavy cargo.» What does emergency suggest? | A quiet day at the park | *A serious problem that needs quick action | A new game | A birthday party
test: Which form of jettison shows that something happened in the past? | jettisons | *jettisoned | jettisoning | jettison
exam: Jessie says, «We need to jettison the idea.» Which word is closest in meaning to jettison? | Remember | *Drop | Copy | Keep
